{"name":"Colossus","hex":"#625c91","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"colossus","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A statue of gigantic size. The name was especially applied to certain famous statues in antiquity, as the Colossus of Nero in Rome and the Colossus of Rhodes, one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World.","Any creature or thing of gigantic size."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/colossus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Statue","blocks":[{"text":"A statue is a free-standing sculpture in which the realistic, full-length figures of persons or animals are carved or cast in a durable material such as wood, metal, glass, marble, or stone. Typical statues are life-sized or close to life-size. A sculpture that represents persons or animals in full figure, but that is small enough to lift and carry is a statuette or figurine, whilst those that are more than twice life-size are regarded as colossal statues."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Lincoln_Memorial_statue_at_night_2011.jpg/330px-Lincoln_Memorial_statue_at_night_2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Statue"},{"title":"List of tallest statues","blocks":[{"text":"This list of tallest statues includes completed statues that are at least 50 m tall. The height values in this list are measured to the highest part of the human or animal figure, but exclude the height of any mast, spire, or other structure that extends higher than the tallest figure in the monument."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_tallest_statues"},{"title":"Colossus (character)","blocks":[{"text":"Colossus is a character appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. Created by writer Len Wein and artist Dave Cockrum, he first appeared in Giant-Size X-Men #1."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/26/Colossus-AvX_Consequences.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colossus_(character)"},{"title":"Colossus (data center)","blocks":[{"text":"Colossus is the name used for a cluster of data centers developed by xAI in the Memphis, Tennessee–Southaven, Mississippi area. The original facility, Colossus 1, began construction in 2024 at a former Electrolux plant in South Memphis and became operational in July–September 2024. Its primary purpose was to train the company's chatbot Grok; it also supported other projects associated with Elon Musk, including the social network X and SpaceX."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colossus_(data_center)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Urfa_man.jpg/500px-Urfa_man.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Urfa_man.jpg/500px-Urfa_man.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Urfa Man, a 1.80 metres (5 ft 11 in) of standstone developed in c. 9,000 BC and now housed at Şanlıurfa Museum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUrfa_man.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Queen_Hatshepsut%2C_1479-1458_BCE_%28GEM%29.jpg/500px-Queen_Hatshepsut%2C_1479-1458_BCE_%28GEM%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Queen_Hatshepsut%2C_1479-1458_BCE_%28GEM%29.jpg/1280px-Queen_Hatshepsut%2C_1479-1458_BCE_%28GEM%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Queen_Hatshepsut%2C_1479-1458_BCE_%28GEM%29.jpg/500px-Queen_Hatshepsut%2C_1479-1458_BCE_%28GEM%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Statue of Queen Hatshepsut in the Grand Egyptian Museum in